
This new version aides in recovering ERASEd disk files, and in salvaging
data from bad HDAs.

There are now commands to:

1) Search for disk blocks containing specified text strings or pointer
   block numbers.

2) Create a file from a disk block. This allows one to retreive data
   from a file that has been erased.

3) Copy a minidisk block-by-block to another minidisk. This is useful
   if some heads of an HDA are bad. We used it recently to recover most
   of the files on a minidisk on a bad HDA.
